      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-3019",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\u27e816,\\,2,\\,-2\u27e9+\u27e82,\\,-4,\\,2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e848,\\,6,\\,-6\u27e9+\u27e82,\\,-4,\\,2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e850,2,-4\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3019.json",
          "file_sha256": "b4325214312d2fe2a72d3d0a7c6ae0ef7fc9e2f2ffbf86b7e22b0d47f8fd7959"
        }
