      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8688",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\u27e8-3,\\,2,\\,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,-2,\\,-1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+\u27e81,\\,-1,\\,1\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}\u27e81,\\,-1,\\,1\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,-2,\\,-1\u27e9+\u27e8t,\\,-t,\\,t\u27e9{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\u27e83,\\,-2,\\,-1\u27e9+\u27e82,\\,-2,\\,2\u27e9\\text{\u00a0} \\\\  & =\u27e85,\\,-4,\\,1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-8688.json",
