    {
      "question": "e-3020",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "182503fe9a705d5c6171bfd5b37f2e7215f8daa5dd5788a5c3e95f985c2d2138",
      "new_sha256": "330b1861e3ee1182f8060e23603a0b2df41ccf1429208793a82cea4df9e533c7",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-3020",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,2,\\,6\u27e9-\u27e8\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3020.json",
          "file_sha256": "203f27b71cbdb193ed73d4978a08ef8e94342401b0256735cf0a638d2578da86"
