    {
      "question": "e-3021",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "b4112086c80ebc2646eea759a585653d3725ba9d959d670bc25ef024deb470f8",
      "new_sha256": "eee5869fd6151a48b61d8f74841ef8195bf56d6055b346f5ccbf0ea3e9066f9f",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-3021",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3021.json",
          "file_sha256": "c03273a86020ea3e0bd108a41c3391276aa81a13a9aeed0d709722553282641e"
